briefing =
    FICTIONAL RED SEA OPERATION — CONVOY SHIELD

    A civilian relief convoy must cross a contested sea lane. No real-world incident, leader, force, or attack is depicted.

    Choose the short exposed central passage or the longer southern safety route. Keep the radar picket separated from the escort so it can illuminate threat sectors without continuously revealing the main force. Protect the relief freighters and tanker, recover survivors, stabilize a disabled vessel, and contain any tanker fire before it becomes an environmental disaster.

    Preserve the difficulty-specific relief cargo threshold and escort the surviving vessels through the eastern evacuation corridor. Maritime intelligence west of the corridor is optional, but securing it will improve warning time.

